  "note": "Chapter 23 (book pp.728-771, PDF pp.731-774) has 711 questions, by far the largest chapter in the book, organised into lettered sub-sections (Type A squares/rectangles, Type B circles+triangles, Type C quadrilaterals, Type D cost-rate, Type E ratio-of-areas, Type F percentage-change, then Type G onward which turns to 3D solids - see ry7300-ch23-mensuration-3d). This file covers only the 2D portion. Given the extreme internal redundancy (the same formula re-applied to different numbers over and over), a heavily trimmed selection was kept: 39 of the roughly 360 2D questions (Types A-F plus a handful of 2D stragglers in the real-exam-dated SSC CPO 2016 tail), spanning every distinct 2D technique found - squares/rectangles (diagonal-area, scaling, combining, wire-bending), wheels and meshed gears, circles (touching circles, radius-vs-area growth), triangles (Heron's formula, equilateral incircle/circumcircle, centroid/medians, medial triangle), quadrilaterals (rhombus, hexagon, parallelogram, trapezium), percentage change in area or perimeter, cost of flooring a path, and regular-polygon diagonals. The book gives no single compact answer-key table for the 2D section's early pages (solutions are worked individually); every answer here was verified by independent recomputation from the question's own numbers, matching exactly one of the four printed options.",
